      "title": "Note: Krea 2",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Krea 2 (raw)\n\nCanonical Krea 2 settings: 52 steps, CFG 3.5, euler / simple, empty negative, 1216x832, fp8 weights. Prompt: quality prefix, medium first, text clause, key concepts repeated at the end.\n\nRTX 5070 Laptop: native 283 s, Automatic (3 stages, \u0394 0.05) 215 s, Manual (0.5x to step 26) 183 s.\n\n## SPEED on an image model\n\nAll SPEED nodes here use **noise_policy = coupled_full_grid**.\n\n1. **Harvest** (muted): run once, paste the report's values into Automatic.\n2. **Automatic** (active): already set to this prompt's harvested values. At \u0394 0.005 the low-resolution stage ends in the first steps, so it saves little; \u0394 0.05 is the useful setting for images.\n3. **Manual** (muted): swap in for Automatic.\n\n`coupled_full_grid` draws the noise from the seed as SamplerCustomAdvanced does, so SPEED keeps a native\nrun's composition at the same seed; small details such as an object count can still change.\n"
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "## Krea 2 (raw)\n\nCanonical Krea 2 settings: 52 steps, CFG 3.5, euler / simple, empty negative, 1216x832, fp8 weights. Prompt: quality prefix, medium first, text clause, key concepts repeated at the end.\n\nRTX 5070 Laptop: native 283 s, Automatic (3 stages, \u0394 0.05) 215 s, Manual (0.5x to step 26) 183 s.\n\n## SPEED on an image model\n\nAll SPEED nodes here use **noise_policy = coupled_full_grid**.\n\n1. **Harvest** (muted): run once, paste the report's values into Automatic.\n2. **Automatic** (active): already set to this prompt's harvested values. At \u0394 0.005 the low-resolution stage ends in the first steps, so it saves little; \u0394 0.05 is the useful setting for images.\n3. **Manual** (muted): swap in for Automatic.\n\n`coupled_full_grid` draws the noise from the seed as SamplerCustomAdvanced does, so SPEED keeps a native\nrun's composition at the same seed; small details such as an object count can still change.\n"
      },
      "color": "#222",
      "bgcolor": "#000"
    },
